#: source/architecture/architecture.md:1
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:3
msgid ""
"This chapter describes how Nix works. It should help users understand why "
"Nix behaves as it does, and it should help developers understand how to "
"modify Nix and how to write similar tools."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:6
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:8
msgid ""
"Nix consists of [hierarchical layers](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Multitier_architecture#Layers)."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:12
msgid ""
"The following [concept map](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concept_map) shows "
"its main components (rectangles), the objects they operate on (rounded "
"rectangles), and their interactions (connecting phrases):"
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:55
msgid ""
"At the top is the [command line interface](../command-ref/index.md) that "
"drives the underlying layers."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:57
msgid ""
"The [Nix language](../language/index.md) evaluator transforms Nix "
"expressions into self-contained _build plans_, which are used to derive "
"_build results_ from referenced _build inputs_."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:59
msgid ""
"The command line interface and Nix expressions are what users deal with most."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:61
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:63
msgid ""
"The Nix language itself does not have a notion of _packages_ or "
"_configurations_. As far as we are concerned here, the inputs and results of "
"a build plan are just data."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:66
msgid ""
"Underlying the command line interface and the Nix language evaluator is the "
"[Nix store](../store/index.md), a mechanism to keep track of build plans, "
"data, and references between them. It can also execute build plans to "
"produce new data, which are made available to the operating system as files."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:69
msgid ""
"A build plan itself is a series of _build tasks_, together with their build "
"inputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:71
msgid ""
"**Important** A build task in Nix is called [store derivation](../glossary."
"md#gloss-store-derivation)."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:74
msgid ""
"Each build task has a special build input executed as _build instructions_ "
"in order to perform the build. The result of a build task can be input to "
"another build task."
msgstr ""

#: source/architecture/architecture.md:77
msgid ""
"The following [data flow diagram](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data-"
"flow_diagram) shows a build plan for illustration. Build inputs used as "
"instructions to a build task are marked accordingly:"
msgstr ""
